// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  FARM IDENTITY DOMAIN — P3.4: claiming a farm by its ЕИК
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
//  GAP-09 multi-file schema: new domain file. Generator + datasource
//  remain in base.prisma.
//
//  WHY NOT social.prisma. That file's header states its models are
//  PLATFORM-scoped on purpose and that "there is no `tenantId` here, and
//  the RLS classification is deliberately not the tenant-scoped one".
//  `FarmIdentityClaim` is tenant-scoped, so adding it there would make
//  that paragraph false — and a file-level invariant that silently stops
//  holding is worse than a second file.
//
//  WHAT A CLAIM IS. A tenant asserting "this ЕИК is my farm". It is not
//  proof: a claim starts PENDING and only a staff verification (P3.9)
//  moves it to VERIFIED. `FarmProfile.eik` is written ONLY from a
//  VERIFIED claim, as v2 ciphertext under the tenant DEK, never from the
//  free-edit PUT — so this table is the sole gate on that field.
//
//  WHY THE PLAINTEXT ЕИК IS NOT HERE. The row stores only a blind index.
//  A claim table is the one place in the product that necessarily holds a
//  row per farm identity somebody typed, including identities that were
//  typed wrongly, speculatively, or by someone with no connection to the
//  farm. Keeping the plaintext would make it the best enumeration target
//  in the database. The index is an HMAC under `LOOKUP_HMAC_KEY` with its
//  own HKDF info (`LookupKind = 'eik'`), so it is neither reversible
//  without the key nor comparable against the `email` index.

/// One tenant's assertion that an ЕИК is its farm.
///
/// ## The uniqueness rule, and why the database owns it
///
/// At most one VERIFIED claim may exist per ЕИК. That is enforced by a
/// PARTIAL unique index — `(eikHash) WHERE status = 'VERIFIED'` — created
/// in this model's migration, because Prisma cannot express a partial
/// unique index declaratively.
///
/// It has to be the database rather than a read-then-insert check in the
/// usecase, for a reason specific to this table: RLS scopes reads to the
/// calling tenant, so a pre-insert "does anyone already hold this ЕИК?"
/// query run as `app_user` sees ZERO rows whenever the incumbent belongs
/// to someone else — which is always, in the only case that matters. The
/// check would pass, the insert would succeed, and two farms would hold
/// one verified identity with nothing having failed. A constraint is
/// enforced on the heap, below the policies, so it sees the conflict the
/// query cannot.
///
/// This is also why a collision is only observable as a write failure
/// (Prisma `P2002`) and never as a lookup result, which is what keeps the
/// enumeration property in P3.4 intact: the caller learns their own claim
/// did not become verified, not who holds it.
///
/// ## The collision resolves against the CLAIMANT, not the incumbent
///
/// A colliding claim becomes DISPUTED. The existing VERIFIED claim is left
/// alone. The reverse — demoting both to DISPUTED — reads as even-handed
/// and is a griefing primitive: anyone who can type a verified farm's ЕИК
/// could knock it out of verified status, repeatedly, with no access to
/// anything belonging to that farm. A claim is not evidence against an
/// already-verified one.
///
/// ## A rotation window this index cannot see
///
/// `eikHash` stores the hash under the CURRENT lookup key. During a
/// `LOOKUP_HMAC_KEY` rotation, `hashForLookupCandidates` reads under both
/// the current and previous key, but a row written before the rotation
/// still carries the OLD hash — so two claims on the same ЕИК, one either
/// side of the rotation, are two different values and the partial unique
/// index does not relate them. The guarantee is therefore "one VERIFIED
/// claim per ЕИК per key generation", and closing the gap is the
/// verification path's job: it must look the ЕИК up with the full
/// candidate set before promoting anything to VERIFIED, and re-hash the
/// row it promotes. Do not read the index as the whole guarantee.
model FarmIdentityClaim {
  id       String @id @default(cuid())
  /// The claiming farm. A plain column rather than a relation, matching
  /// every other tenant-scoped model here, and the column RLS scopes by.
  tenantId String
  /// Blind index over the ЕИК: `hashForLookup(eik, 'eik')`. 64 hex chars.
  /// Never the plaintext — see the file header.
  eikHash  String
  status   FarmIdentityClaimStatus @default(PENDING)
  /// The person who made the claim, for the audit trail and so a staff
  /// reviewer can see who to contact. Not `app.user_id`-scoped: the claim
  /// belongs to the farm, and a colleague must be able to see it.
  claimedByUserId String
  /// Set when a reviewer promotes the claim. Null in every other state,
  /// including DISPUTED — a disputed claim was never verified.
  verifiedAt DateTime?
  /// Set when a claim collides with an existing VERIFIED one. Kept
  /// separately from `updatedAt` so a sweep can find disputes by age
  /// without inferring the reason for the last write.
  disputedAt DateTime?
  createdAt  DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt  DateTime @updatedAt

  /// Reads are "this farm's claims" and "is this ЕИК claimed"; both are
  /// indexed. The partial UNIQUE index on `eikHash` lives in the
  /// migration and is a constraint, not a substitute for this one — it
  /// covers only VERIFIED rows, so it cannot serve a lookup that must
  /// also see PENDING and DISPUTED.
  @@index([tenantId])
  @@index([eikHash])
  /// The P3.9 review queue: `WHERE status = 'PENDING' ORDER BY "createdAt"`,
  /// CROSS-tenant. Neither index above serves it — the queue does not filter
  /// by tenant at all, which is the point of a platform review surface, so
  /// `[tenantId]` leads with a column the query never mentions.
  @@index([status, createdAt])
}

/// A claim's lifecycle. There is no `UNVERIFIED`: the absence of a claim
/// and a claim that failed are different facts, and both must produce the
/// same response to a caller (P3.4), which is a property of the ROUTE, not
/// of this enum.
enum FarmIdentityClaimStatus {
  /// Submitted, awaiting staff verification. The default.
  PENDING
  /// Verified by staff. At most one per ЕИК per key generation; the only
  /// state from which `FarmProfile.eik` may be written.
  VERIFIED
  /// Collided with an existing VERIFIED claim. Terminal without staff
  /// action — see the model docblock on why the incumbent is not demoted.
  DISPUTED
  /// Rejected by a reviewer. Distinct from DISPUTED: a rejection is a
  /// judgement about this claim, a dispute is a fact about another one.
  REJECTED
}
